x86_64-windows  a different refusal answers first here, and it is broader: a destructible local and a `try` in one function is refused function-wide for this target, body or handler, because a Microsoft cleanup is a funclet and a state in the FH3 tables rather than a row in a call-site list. So this case cannot measure the handler-only refusal on this target - it never reaches it. Both Itanium targets give the message the `.error` names. See try-body-local.notarget for the same lag stated from the other side.
